# #5841, reproduced: a stale duplicate of the donor arms after the split; ClaimRowAsync
# writes row + 1 and supersedes the bump, and its epoch-only write of a moved key is
# allocated above the receiver's close head.
MODULE: HandOffBoundStaleDonorArmsAfterSplit5841
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: #5841 exactly: the claim writes row + 1 with no staleness check, and the split bumps only if its own activation claimed
PERTURBS: ClaimCheck
BOUNDS: WithStaleDonor = TRUE, WithPreArm = TRUE, MaxWindows = 1, WithRestart = FALSE

--- FIND
    /\ dst' = IF sNarrowed THEN "stale" ELSE "claimed"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the claim does not read the leaf state.
    /\ dst' = "claimed"
--- END

--- FIND
SplitBumps(read) == read > 0
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: only an armed splitting activation bumps.
SplitBumps(read) == liveArmed
--- END
